<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Caltabellotta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1302">1302</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">Sicilian Vespers</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of Caltabellotta, signed on 31 August 1302 at Caltabellotta in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, ended the War of the Sicilian Vespers between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capetian-house-of-anjou">Angevins of Naples</a> and the Aragonese. Frederick III kept the island for his lifetime with the title King of Trinacria, while the Angevin Charles II kept the mainland Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. The island was to return to the Angevins on Frederick's death, but this never happened.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-caltabellotta.jpg" alt="Peace of Caltabellotta" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LuckyLisp · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pace_di_caltabellotta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
